<title>JAPAN: Green Cross gets Japan okay for Chiron HIV therapy.</title>
<headline>Green Cross gets Japan okay for Chiron HIV therapy.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Green Cross Corp said on Friday a Japanese government advisory pannel approved the use of an anti-HIV gene therapy product, HIV-IT(V), now under development by a division of U.S.-based Chiron Corp.</p>
<p>The company is now waiting for the Ministry of Health and Welfare's formal approval, a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The new treatment was jointly developed with Kumamoto University in Japan, the spokesman said.</p>
</text>
